---
description: Defines the standard format and requirements for creating `.mdc` files.
globs: **/*.mdc
alwaysApply: false
---
# mdc-creation.mdc

meta:
  name: MDC Creation Standards
  description: >
    Defines the standard format and requirements for creating Model Definition Card (.mdc) files.
    Ensures consistency and machine-readability of project rules and constraints.
    Used by LLMs to understand and apply project standards.

rules:
  - when: file.created
    match: "**/*.mdc"
    then:
      - "Must use kebab-case for filenames (e.g., 'mdc-creation.mdc')"
      - "Must include a clear, concise description in the meta section"
      - "Description must explain the purpose and scope of the MDC file"
      - "Description must be specific enough for LLMs to determine applicability"
      - "Description should be one or two sentences maximum"
      - "Description must be in plain language, avoiding technical jargon"
      - "Description must be enclosed in '>' for multi-line support"

  - when: file.modified
    match: "**/*.mdc"
    then:
      - "Must maintain kebab-case in filenames"
      - "Must preserve description in meta section"
      - "Must ensure description remains clear and relevant"
      - "Must update description if MDC purpose changes"
      - "Must not use edit_file or edit_tool for MDC modifications"
      - "Must use structured YAML libraries (PyYAML, ruamel.yaml) for YAML portions"
      - "Must use markdown libraries (markdown-it-py, mistune, panflute) for markdown portions"
      - "Must validate YAML syntax before applying changes"
      - "Must preserve file structure and formatting"

  - when: file.created
    match: "**/*.mdc"
    then:
      - "Must follow YAML syntax"
      - "Must include meta section with name and description"
      - "Must include rules section with when, match, and then clauses"
      - "Must use consistent indentation (2 spaces)"
      - "Must use double quotes for strings containing special characters"
      - "Must use single quotes for simple strings"

  - when: file.modified
    match: "**/*.mdc"
    then:
      - "Must maintain kebab-case in filenames"
      - "Must preserve description in meta section"
      - "Must ensure description remains clear and relevant"
      - "Must update description if MDC purpose changes"
      - "Must not use edit_file or edit_tool for MDC modifications"
      - "Must use structured YAML libraries (PyYAML, ruamel.yaml) for YAML portions"
      - "Must use markdown libraries (markdown-it-py, mistune, panflute) for markdown portions"
      - "Must validate YAML syntax before applying changes"
      - "Must preserve file structure and formatting"
      - "Must use appropriate string quotes"

  - when: pr.created
    then:
      - "Must review MDC file format"
      - "Must verify description clarity and relevance"
      - "Must check rule applicability"
      - "Must validate YAML syntax"
      - "Must ensure consistent formatting"

rationale: >
  These requirements ensure that:
  - MDC files are consistent and machine-readable
  - Rules are properly integrated with the project model
  - Rules can be validated and enforced
  - Rules are maintainable and well-documented
  - Rules follow project standards

---

This rule helps ensure MDC files meet project standards for consistency and integration.
